					<Item class="StringValue" referent="365">
						<Properties>
							<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Facet documentation

Open the [documentation map](nodes/Map.md).
Run `lute run tools/facet docs` to read the map.

`Facet.MenuCommand` types a command menu item. `Facet.RadialAction<V>` types a
radial command. See [menu items](nodes/Menu-and-SplitButton.items.md) and
[radial items](nodes/RadialMenu.items.md).

Move an existing live application onto a world surface with
[DiegeticScreen](nodes/DiegeticScreen.reference.md).

Use [SpatialGrid](nodes/SpatialGrid.reference.md) for keyed inventory items
with explicit cell footprints. `Facet.SpatialGridSpec<V, K>` types the control;
`Facet.SpatialPlacement` types both item positions and `DropInfo.placement`.

Use [custom transitions](nodes/Custom-transitions.md) to bind native transforms
to retained presentation progress. `Facet.Transition` and
`Facet.TransitionContext` type the options and callback context.
For pointer-driven transitions, bind a nullable Compose cell to
`Transition.progress`; native drag input holds it and clearing it resumes
the control's settlement.

Use [ButtonGuide](nodes/ButtonGuide.reference.md) for a console button legend
of commands that have no control of their own. `Facet.ButtonGuideProps` types
the control and `Facet.ButtonGuideEntry` types one entry. The Sheet `guide`
option places one on the sheet's bottom edge, and the `buttonGuides` app
option lets players hide every guide.
]]></string>
							<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
							<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
							<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
							<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
							<string name="Name">api.md</string>
							<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
							<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
							<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
							<UniqueId name="UniqueId">1f5f3983a820f33d0aedc38900000549</UniqueId>
						</Properties>
					</Item>
					<Item class="StringValue" referent="366">
						<Properties>
							<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Facet's architecture rules

1. Only Compose owns scene construction, reactive bindings and lifetime.
2. Roblox owns layout, text editing and measurement, scrolling, selection,
   native input transport, drag detection and styling.
3. Facet owns reusable control behavior, semantic styling and adaptive
   decisions.
4. A control returns a native Instance and uses the Compose runtime of the
   caller.
5. Native properties and Compose keys pass through. There is no parallel
   vocabulary.
6. Behavioral options are explicit. An unknown native property fails at the
   engine boundary. Silently dropping options is not validation.
7. The model owns durable state. Controls send commands through callbacks.
8. Modal eligibility, focus restoration, cancellation, accessibility and
   resource cleanup are behavioral requirements. They are not optional
   decoration.
9. Current examples and tools use one supported API. There are no
   compatibility facades.
10. Code is self-documenting. Keep executable directives and required legal
    notices. Put explanations in focused public documentation and named tests.

A native engine double proves the binding and ownership policy. Only a live
engine proves layout and input behavior. A passing subset is not full evidence.
]]></string>
