						<Item class="StringValue" referent="389">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Button.card

Run a player action.

Inside an app mount, set `local UI = app.UI`.

```luau
UI.Button "Button" { label = "Save", onActivate = function() print("Save") end }
```

Key options: `label`, `role`, `appearance`, `enabled`, `busy`.

Use onActivate for activation.
To fill a VStack's width, set `align = "stretch"` on that stack.
Use a `UI.fill()` child to share an HStack's width.
Use native `Size` for an explicit width. See [Layout-options](Layout-options.md).

Related controls: [Controls](Controls.md).

Open:

- [Button.reference](Button.reference.md)
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Button.card.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">1f5f3983a820f33d0aedc38900000561</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="390">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Button.disclose

Button.disclose option values and behavior.

- `disclose`: `true` lets a player read the whole label of a text Button
  that truncates. With an authored width the label keeps one line and
  truncates at the end instead of wrapping. The label shows in the help panel (named `Disclosure`) on the
  same routes as `help`, only while the engine reports that the text does not
  fit (`TextFits`). While it shows, `help` waits: the full value comes first.
- `compactLabel`: an alternative string or readable. The button uses it when a
  plain text button cannot fit its full label. It does not apply to icon, image
  or subtitle buttons.


The pointer callbacks are `onPointerDown`, `onPointerUp` and `onPointerCancel`.
Each callback works alone. `onPointerCancel` runs once when a held pointer
leaves the button, the Button is destroyed, or its Compose owner is disposed.
Cancellation clears the held state and stops repetition before the callback.
A normal release calls `onPointerUp` without a cancellation.

A text Button with a bounded width truncates its label at the end when the
label does not fit its box. A Button whose width follows its label does not
truncate. A text Button or Toggle with an authored `Size` that has a width, and no
authored `AutomaticSize`, wraps its label inside that width and grows in
height. With an authored `TextTruncate` other than `None`, it keeps one line
and truncates instead. An icon Button with an authored width (and no image
or row) keeps that width, and its label truncates at the end. A Button with
`subtitle` or `hint` and an authored width also keeps that width: the label
and the subtitle wrap inside it, and the Button grows in height.
This also applies to a reactive `Size` with `AutomaticSize = None` or `Y`.
With no authored `AutomaticSize`, a reactive `Size` selects `Y` while its X
scale or offset is positive, and `XY` while neither is positive. The plain
caption's wrapping follows that width. An explicit `AutomaticSize` wins.
Its content stays inside the padding, and the label shrinks before the icon.
An authored width never leaves less than one `control` em for the label inside
the padding and the theme carve: the Button grows to that minimum. The minimum
also holds each icon and the gap after it.
Without an authored width, it hugs its label.
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Button.disclose.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">1f5f3983a820f33d0aedc38900000562</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="391">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Button.label

`label`, `onActivate`, `enabled`, `disabled` and `busy` define the action. A
disabled or busy button cannot activate. With `repeatDelay` or
`repeatInterval` (the defaults are `0.4` and `0.1` seconds), a held button
activates again after `repeatDelay` and then every `repeatInterval`, for a
mouse, a touch, Return, Space or ButtonA. The repeat follows the frame clock
only while the button is held, and it stops on release, when the pointer
leaves, and when the button is disabled or hidden. The Stepper buttons and the
NumberInput `stepButtons` repeat in this way. `shortcut` supplies
a key code and optional modifiers. `dialogAction` is `default` or `cancel`.

A Button keeps the height of its `controlSize` when its `Size` has no height
and its `AutomaticSize` grows on the Y axis. For example,
`Size = UDim2.new(1, 0, 0, 0)` gives a full-width button of the control height.

`AutoButtonColor` defaults to `false`. The theme owns hover and press paint.
Set it to `true` to use Roblox automatic button coloring.

Presentation options:

`caption` shows text centred below the Button in the caption type role, for
example the name under a circle icon button in a HUD row. The caption takes
no space in the layout and can be wider than the Button. In a row of
captioned Buttons, set `gap` to at least the widest caption minus the Button
width, for example `gap = "m"` for one-word names under compact circles.
The caption is a native TextLabel inside the Button. It names the Button for
the player and for tools such as `verify --tap`, which press the Button that
holds the matched text. The player presses the Button itself. Keep `label` or
`name` for the accessible name. A caption sets `ClipsDescendants` to `false` on the Button.

`glyph = function(): GuiObject` supplies a native leading visual instead of
`icon`. It runs once in the Button's Compose owner. The native content row
places and sizes the result from the control icon metric; keep `label` for
visible text and `name` for an icon-only accessible name. The result can contain
`UI.Path` controls. The theme applies action, selection and disabled colours
to those paths. Do not set both `glyph` and `icon` or `row.icon`.
]]></string>
