						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="398">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[### Call style

<!-- aliases: Call style | call-style -->

Call-style contract and option values.

Use a dot for fields that are plain functions: `Facet.app`, `app.mount`,
`app.dispose`, `runtime.mount`, `runtime.mountFragment`, `runtime.decorate`
`runtime.spring` and `runtime.tween`. Use a colon for the Compose runtime
methods: `runtime:dispose()`, `runtime:batch(body)`, `runtime:watch(body)`,
`runtime:settle()` and `runtime:pending()`. Compose declares these with `self`,
and the type check rejects the dot form. Cells use a colon:
`cell:set(value)`, `cell:update(fn)` and `cell:peek()`.
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Call-style.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">1f5f3983a820f33d0aedc3890000056a</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="399">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Callout.card

Attach guidance to a control.

Inside an app mount, set `local UI = app.UI`.

```luau
local anchor = UI.Button "Play" { label = "Play" }
local help = UI.Callout "Help" {
  anchor = anchor, title = "Start here", closeButton = true,
  content = function()
    return UI.Text { text = "Try the action.", wrap = true, Size = UDim2.fromScale(1, 0) }
  end,
  actions = { { id = "Try", label = "Try", onActivate = function() print("Try") end } },
  onRetire = function(reason) print(reason) end,
}
UI.VStack "Prompt" { anchor :: unknown, help :: unknown }
```

`actions` takes one or two commands. Each action retires this Callout.
For a sequence, use Back and Next with `closeButton` for dismissal.
The model owns the step. Mount a new Callout when the step changes.

Open [Callout.reference](Callout.reference.md) for options.
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
