						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="430">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Composition.layout

Region measurement, authored sizes and layout boundaries.

- A zone is a native Frame with an `AnchorPoint` and a scale `Position` at
  its edge or corner. A corner, side or `center` zone hugs its regions and
  stacks them in declaration order with a `UIListLayout`.
- The `top` and `bottom` zones put their regions side by side in declaration
  order, in rows that are centred. A region goes to a new row only when it
  does not fit beside the regions before it in the room of the zone. The zone
  is as wide as its widest row. Its height is the height of its rows and the
  `gap` between them. A native `UIListLayout` with `Wraps` makes the rows.
  Landed `topbar` regions are one column at the start of the `top` row.
- A region whose content measures zero, such as a scoreboard that shows only
  in a match, takes no room and no `gap`. When another region of its zone has
  content, the empty region is hidden. A presented control in it, such as a
  Sheet, still shows.
- The screen has three lanes of equal width: left, center and right. A side
  zone stays at its edge. In the top and bottom rows, when the center zone of
  that row is empty, a corner zone can use the width that the other corner
  leaves, minus `gap`. Otherwise, and always in the middle row, which keeps
  the view clear, a side zone must fit its third.
- A center-lane zone (`top`, `center`, `bottom`) can also use the width that
  the side zones of its row leave free. Its width must not exceed the full
  width minus twice the wider side zone of that row and twice `gap`. When
  both side zones of its row are empty, it can use the full width. Thus a
  wide `top` or `bottom` region fits on a phone when the corners of its row
  are empty or narrow. When the side zones of its row squeeze a center zone
  that fits the row alone, the side regions that are wider than the room the
  center leaves also count as not fitting. Thus rank decides: a rank 3 corner
  steps down before a rank 1 race bar, and a rank 1 corner keeps its form
  while a rank 2 center region steps down.
- The center-lane zones draw above the side zones (`ZIndex` 2).
  Thus a side region cannot hide a center callout.
- The zones of one lane must not overlap vertically. The `center` zone stays centred and keeps `gap` from the
  zones above and below it.
- At ten feet, a Composition that is the root of its ScreenGui keeps every
  zone inside the TV safe area: it adds the environment's `overscanInsets` to
  its padding. A Composition inside `UI.Screen` uses the margins of the Screen.
  Do not offset a zone by hand.

Open [Composition.layout.step-down](Composition.layout.step-down.md) for form selection,
zone fallback, fit warnings and resize motion.
Open [Composition.adaptation](Composition.adaptation.md) for `topbar` layout.
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Composition.layout.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">1f5f3983a820f33d0aedc3890000058a</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="431">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Composition.layout.step-down

Form selection, zone fallback, fit warnings and resize motion.

- Every form stays mounted in its own `Form<n>` Frame. Roblox measures each
  form, also a hidden one. Only the Frame of the chosen form is visible, so a
  form keeps its own `Visible`. The region has the `FacetForm` attribute.
- When a lane does not fit, the region with the highest rank in the zones
  that do not fit shows its next form. After its last form, a region with
  `mayDrop` hides. With equal ranks, the later region gives way first.
- When a zone is too wide, only its regions that are wider than the room of
  the zone give way. A narrow region cannot make the zone narrower. A `top`
  or `bottom` zone first wraps a region to a new row. Its regions give way
  only when a single region is too wide or the rows are too tall.
- The composition repeats this until every lane fits or no region can give
  way. It never scales content down.
- A `top` or `bottom` zone can remain too wide for the space between its row's
  corner zones after no region can give way. It then moves below the top
  corners, or above the bottom corners, and uses the full width.
  The composition resolves again from the richest forms.
  The `left` and `right` zones that the moved zone covers give way first.
- A region can still fail to fit at its last form when nothing else can give
  way. The composition then warns once in the output and names the region.
  Give that region a smaller form, `mayDrop = true` or a higher rank number.
- Each Composition lays out only its own regions. Two Compositions are on
  one screen when their layers are the same or have the same parent. When
  two Compositions on one screen place visible regions in the same zone for
  two seconds, the composition warns once for that pair and zone. A disabled
  layer and a region in the top bar strip do not count. Put the HUD in one
  Composition.
- The decision uses only the measured sizes and the size of the composition.
  Thus a rotation, a resize or a text size change gives the same forms as a
  new mount of the same size.
- The composition measures each form with its scale. To animate part of a
  region with `UIScale`, put it on an inner frame inside a holder of fixed
  size. This keeps the animation from changing the region's size or form.
- When the size of the composition changes, for example on a rotation, a
  region that changes form scales from 0.94 to 1 in 0.15 seconds, Cubic
  Out, from the edge of its zone. The first layout after a mount does not
  move. Its measurement holds until the motion ends,
  so the motion cannot change the decision. Reduced motion removes the motion.
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
