						<Item class="StringValue" referent="878">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[# Typewriter.props
Options: name: type = default. omitted uses the control or theme default; required has no default.
controls: TypewriterControls? = omitted
direction: ("auto" | "ltr" | "rtl")? = omitted
disclose: boolean? = omitted
lines: number? = omitted
onRevealed: (() -> ())? = omitted
ref: ((TextLabel) -> ())? = omitted
reveal: "auto"? = omitted
rich: boolean? = omitted
role: Value<"secondary" | "content">? = omitted
text: ValueString = required
textAlign: Value<("start" | "center" | "end")>? = omitted
textRole: Value<("caption" | "label" | "body" | "heading" | "title" | "control" | "strong" | "numeral")>? = omitted
textSize: (number | ("caption" | "label" | "body" | "heading" | "title" | "control" | "strong" | "numeral") | ("fit" | { fit: { cap: (number | ("caption" | "label" | "body" | "heading" | "title" | "control" | "strong" | "numeral"))?, floor: (number | ("caption" | "label" | "body" | "heading" | "title" | "control" | "strong" | "numeral"))? } }))? = omitted
tint: Value<Color3>? = omitted
truncate: ("end" | "middle")? = omitted
wrap: ValueBoolean? = omitted
TypewriterControls = { revealed: Readable<boolean>?, finish: (() -> ())?, }]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Typewriter.props.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">1f5f3983a820f33d0aedc3890000074a</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="879">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[### Typewriter

<!-- aliases: Typewriter | typewriter -->

`UI.Typewriter(spec: TypewriterProps) -> TextLabel` takes the Text options and
reveals the full `text` through native `MaxVisibleGraphemes`. It never slices
the string. It counts graphemes in engine `ContentText`, so rich-text tags and
entities do not add reveal steps. A new text value restarts the reveal.
`MaxVisibleGraphemes`, a middle cut and `reveal = "auto"` are refused.

The theme tokens `motion.typewriter.grapheme` (seconds per grapheme, default
0.035) and `motion.typewriter.pause` (initial seconds, default 0) set timing.
The interval must be positive and the pause must be nonnegative. The neutral
theme supplies missing tokens. At motion level `limited` or `none`, the whole
line shows at once. Text styles and the font follow the theme.

`onRevealed()` runs once when the line finishes, including an empty line,
Skip or reduced motion. Pass a `TypewriterControls` table as `controls` to
get `revealed: Readable<boolean>` and `finish: () -> ()`. `finish()` shows
the whole line at once. Repeated calls do not repeat the callback. A new line
resets `revealed`. Unmount cancels the clock and clears the controls fields.

```luau
local reveal: Facet.TypewriterControls = {}
local dialogueLine = Compose.cell("<b>Guide:</b> Follow the lights to the next camp.")
UI.Typewriter "Guide" { text = dialogueLine, rich = true, wrap = true, controls = reveal }
UI.Button { label = "Skip", onActivate = function() if reveal.finish then reveal.finish() end end }
```
]]></string>
								<BinaryString name="AttributesSerialize"></BinaryString>
								<SecurityCapabilities name="Capabilities">0</SecurityCapabilities>
								<bool name="DefinesCapabilities">false</bool>
								<UniqueId name="HistoryId">00000000000000000000000000000000</UniqueId>
								<string name="Name">Typewriter.reference.md</string>
								<BinaryString name="SerializedOverrides"></BinaryString>
								<int64 name="SourceAssetId">-1</int64>
								<SharedString name="Tags">yuZpQdnvvUBOTYh1jqZ2cA==</SharedString>
								<UniqueId name="UniqueId">1f5f3983a820f33d0aedc3890000074b</UniqueId>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
						<Item class="StringValue" referent="880">
							<Properties>
								<string name="Value"><![CDATA[### VStack and HStack

<!-- aliases: VStack and HStack | vstack-and-hstack -->

`UI.VStack(spec) -> Frame` stacks its children vertically. `UI.HStack(spec) ->
Frame` stacks them horizontally. Both hug their content by default. Options:
`gap`, `padding`, `align`, `distribute`, `wrap`, `width` and `height`. `wrap`
sets `UIListLayout.Wraps`. The shared props type is `StackProps`.

Bound a form or collection body with `width = "fill"`. A fill-width field
needs a parent with a defined width; placing two such fields in a hugging
HStack does not divide the available width. Stack fields vertically, or give
each a bounded width and use native flex through [fill](fill.md) to share a row.
Use [AdaptiveStack](AdaptiveStack.reference.md) for short intrinsic-width actions
that should turn into a column when they cannot fit.

A stack with `padding` has an edge, so it keeps its children's shadows inside
it. Each side of its `UIPadding` grows by the farthest a direct child's
`UIShadow` reaches past that child on that side (offset, spread and blur). A
themed Button's drop plate is such a shadow. Hidden children and disabled
shadows take no room. A stack without `padding` is not changed.
]]></string>
